---
kind: scene
id: mid.gameCorner
title: The hideout under the Game Corner
on: enterPlace
target: place.gameCorner
once: false
when: "run.lair.cornerHideout != 'cleared'"
---

// CONTRACT BEAT (owned by mid): moves run.lair.cornerHideout to found on the
// first entry and to cleared on the win over gruntCorner, and hands over
// spectralLens (east's ashTowerStairs gate). A small dungeon: the stair guard,
// the vault guard, the scientist, then Admin Corvo. A trainer already beaten
// is skipped on the next attempt; a loss sends the player back upstairs.

## The Game Corner

::bg{location="game-corner" time="night"}
::music{action="change" mood="upbeat" volume="normal"}
@narrator{when="run.lair.cornerHideout == 'hidden'"}: Bells, lights, the rattle of a hundred slot machines. Nobody looks up from their reels.
@narrator{when="run.lair.cornerHideout == 'hidden'"}: At the back, past the prize counter, a grunt in a black cap is leaning on a poster of a grinning Coinpaw, as if the poster needed holding up.
@narrator{when="run.lair.cornerHideout == 'found'"}: The poster at the back is still slightly crooked. Nobody has fixed it.
::set{run.lair.cornerHideout = "found" when="run.lair.cornerHideout == 'hidden'"}

## The stairs

::bg{location="game-corner-basement" time="night"}
::music{action="change" mood="tense" volume="normal"}
@narrator: Behind the poster, a switch. Behind the switch, a staircase down into the cold.
::use{component="trainerBattle" who="cornerGruntDoor" intro="Hey! That poster was supposed to be a secret! Who told you? Was it Hesketh? It was Hesketh." win="Okay, okay! The Admin's downstairs. Don't tell him I let you by." lose="Upstairs. Go play the slots like everybody else." prize="640" when="!holds(defeated(cornerGruntDoor))"}
::next{to="pushedBack" when="!holds(defeated(cornerGruntDoor))"}

## The vault corridor

@narrator: A corridor of steel doors. Crates stamped HELIX CORP. PROPERTY OF THE DIRECTOR are stacked to the ceiling.
::use{component="trainerBattle" who="cornerGruntVault" intro="These crates don't count themselves, and you're not on the list!" win="I lost count. Of my monsters. And the crates." lose="Seven hundred and twelve crates. And one kid, going back up." prize="680" when="!holds(defeated(cornerGruntVault))"}
::next{to="pushedBack" when="!holds(defeated(cornerGruntVault))"}

## The lab

@narrator: A cramped lab. On the bench, under a lamp: a lens in a brass frame, and a monster that should not be visible flickering in it.
::use{component="trainerBattle" who="cornerScientistLoy" intro="Don't touch the lens! It took us a year to make ghosts sit still for it." win="My calibrations! Weeks of calibrations!" lose="Fascinating. You are exactly as weak as I predicted." prize="880" when="!holds(defeated(cornerScientistLoy))"}
::next{to="pushedBack" when="!holds(defeated(cornerScientistLoy))"}

## Admin Corvo

::use{component="trainerBattle" who="gruntCorner" intro="So the Game Corner pays out after all. A child, down my stairs. The Director's vault is off limits, and so, I'm afraid, is daylight." win="Hm. The house doesn't always win. Take the lens, then. It only shows ghosts, and ghosts don't pay." lose="The house always wins. Show the child out." prize="1200"}
::set{run.lair.cornerHideout = "cleared" when="@wonFight"}
<match on="scene.battle.fight.won">
  <when is="true">
    ::use{component="obtain" item="spectralLens"}
    @narrator: Through the lens, the shadows in the corner of the vault have faces. One of them waves.
    @narrator: Corvo's grunts are already hauling crates up a back staircase. By morning the basement is empty, and the poster is straight.
    ::end{reason="hideoutCleared"}
  </when>
  <otherwise>
    @narrator: Two grunts take an arm each and march you back up the stairs.
  </otherwise>
</match>

## Back upstairs

::mark{id="pushedBack"}
::bg{location="game-corner" time="night"}
@narrator: Upstairs, the slot machines are still ringing. Nobody noticed you were gone.
